00:06:50.122 --> 00:06:54.662
DeepSec, published on GitHub, is the place to pop the hood on multi-phase agent security

00:06:54.662 --> 00:06:55.182
auditing.

00:06:55.682 --> 00:07:00.682
A standalone command line harness that keeps persistent state inside a .deepSec directory

00:07:00.682 --> 00:07:06.162
and runs RegEx pre scans before launching high-effort model investigations on every file.

00:07:07.022 --> 00:07:12.822
Optional massive parallelism through Versel Sandboxes covers large repositories, interrupted

00:07:12.822 --> 00:07:19.002
runs resume by skipping files already analyzed and operators pick an AI model with benchmark scores

00:07:19.002 --> 00:07:25.462
and pricing shown during setup. Unlike lighter single repo skills, an independent revalidation stage

00:07:25.462 --> 00:07:31.202
feeds every candidate finding to a fresh verifier agent told to disprove it before any record is

00:07:31.202 --> 00:07:37.342
written to findings.json. That extra pass costs more tokens and more wall clock time in exchange

00:07:37.342 --> 00:07:40.342
for fewer false positives on complex code bases

00:07:40.342 --> 00:07:43.462
and turning thinking to maximum on a large repo

00:07:43.462 --> 00:07:46.042
can run into thousands of dollars of model spend.

00:07:46.302 --> 00:07:49.942
One-off audits on repositories under 100,000 lines

00:07:49.942 --> 00:07:52.902
can use the lighter skills structured six-phase process

00:07:52.902 --> 00:07:55.282
of reconnaissance, coverage-led hunting,

00:07:55.922 --> 00:07:58.302
candidate validation, structured output,

00:07:58.862 --> 00:08:02.022
independent record verification, and target neutral reporting.

00:08:02.642 --> 00:08:05.802
Repeatable, auditable scans across several large repos

00:08:05.802 --> 00:08:11.422
